🚀 Isko ab apply kaise kare?
Agar tumne pehle se kuch files git add kar di hain, toh sirf .gitignore banane se kaam nahi chalega. Tumhe Git ki memory clear karni padegi. Ye commands apne terminal me ek-ek karke chalao:

Step 1: File create karne ke baad, Git ko batao ki nayi rules apply karo:

bash
git add .gitignore
Step 2: Purani memory clear karo (taaki pehle add hui galat files nikal jayein):

bash
git rm -r --cached .
Step 3: Wapas sab add karo (ab ye .gitignore ko padh kar galat files skip kar dega):

bash
git add .
Step 4: Commit karo:

bash
git commit -m "Added .gitignore and cleaned up repository"
Step 5: Push kar do:

bash
git push -u origin main
Ab jab tum GitHub par apna repo refresh karoge, toh tumhara code safe hoga, node_modules aur venv nahi dikhega, aur tumhari .env file bhi hide rahegi! 🚀



